A||||2||james||auto to manual tranny swap
Z||000000||james||06-04-99||06:32 PM||||I have just bought an 84 2M4 with an auto transmission I want to put a 5 speed in it but I don't know if it will fit and I don't know how to hook up the clutch pedal, help!!
Z||000001||LEE498||06-04-99||09:30 PM||||Well, you have to remove the master clinder and booster,remove your windshield wiper motor it's a lot easier to get to the brake booster nuts if you remove it.NOW the fun part under the dash.You'll have to undo the steering rod to take out the steering wheel assembly.The brake pedal assembly has like two or three nuts that has to come lose. NOW the brake pedal assembly has four studs that are about a inch and a quarter long that holds the booster to the fire wall.THIS is the hardest part of the hole swicth over,trying to manover the brake pedal assembly enough to clear the longgg studs it's very very frustrating but it will come, be careful not to pinch the wiring harness. it took me about 30 min to just get the pedal assembly out!!!!! thats  turning and pulling and pushing! To do the hole swicth you'll need trans,trans mounts, axles, clutch lines,computer,shifter and shifter lines basicly you'll need another car for the parts.
Z||000002||Patrick||06-04-99||09:48 PM||||<br>James, save yourself a ton of work. Either be satisfied with the automatic, or buy a Fiero that comes equipped with a manual transmission. No offence, but judging from your questions, I'd say you would be in over your head changing this Fiero over. <p>You may not appreciate this answer now, but down the road you'll thank me.<p> 
